<h2 data-start=3D"93" data-end=3D"117" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"96"=
 data-end=3D"115">1. Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"119" data-end=3D"433" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99interface en li=
gne de commande (CLI - Command Line Interface) est un outil puissant et ess=
entiel pour tout utilisateur de Linux, du d=C3=A9butant =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99ex=
pert. Contrairement aux interfaces graphiques (GUI - Graphical User Interfa=
ce), le CLI permet une interaction directe avec le syst=C3=A8me via des com=
mandes textuelles.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"435" data-end=3D"471" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"43=
9" data-end=3D"469">Pourquoi utiliser le CLI ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"472" data-end=3D"796" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 <strong data-st=
art=3D"474" data-end=3D"492">Contr=C3=B4le total</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s dire=
ct aux fonctionnalit=C3=A9s du syst=C3=A8me.<br data-start=3D"539" data-end=
=3D"542">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"544" data-end=3D"558">Efficacit=C3=A9</stro=
ng> : Ex=C3=A9cution rapide des t=C3=A2ches, sans navigation dans les menus=
.<br data-start=3D"621" data-end=3D"624">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"626" data-end=3D"644">Automatisation</stron=
g> : Utilisation de scripts pour automatiser des t=C3=A2ches r=C3=A9p=C3=A9=
titives.<br data-start=3D"710" data-end=3D"713">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"715" data-end=3D"735">Gestion distante</str=
ong> : Possibilit=C3=A9 d=E2=80=99administrer un serveur =C3=A0 distance vi=
a SSH.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"801" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"803" data-end=3D"840" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"80=
6" data-end=3D"838">2. Acc=C3=A9der au Terminal Linux</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"842" data-end=3D"920" class=3D"">Le terminal est l=E2=80=
=99application qui permet d=E2=80=99entrer des commandes dans le CLI.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"954" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"92=
6" data-end=3D"952">2.1 Ouvrir un terminal</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D"1293" class=3D"">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong dat=
a-start=3D"958" data-end=3D"980">Sous Ubuntu/Debian</strong> : <code data-s=
tart=3D"983" data-end=3D"999">Ctrl + Alt + T</code><br data-start=3D"999" d=
ata-end=3D"1002">
=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=3D"1005" data-end=3D"1029">Sous Fedora/Open=
SUSE</strong> : Rechercher "Terminal" dans le menu.<br data-start=3D"1067" =
data-end=3D"1070">
=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=3D"1073" data-end=3D"1092">Sous Arch Linux<=
/strong> : <code data-start=3D"1095" data-end=3D"1104">Konsole</code>, <cod=
e data-start=3D"1106" data-end=3D"1113">Xterm</code>, <code data-start=3D"1=
115" data-end=3D"1131">Gnome Terminal</code> selon l=E2=80=99environnement =
de bureau.<br data-start=3D"1164" data-end=3D"1167">
=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=3D"1170" data-end=3D"1204">En mode texte un=
iquement (TTY)</strong> : <code data-start=3D"1207" data-end=3D"1224">Ctrl =
+ Alt + F1</code> =C3=A0 <code data-start=3D"1227" data-end=3D"1231">F6</co=
de> (pour revenir =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99interface graphique : <code data-start=
=3D"1272" data-end=3D"1289">Ctrl + Alt + F7</code>).</p>
