<h2 data-start=3D"82" data-end=3D"106" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"85"=
 data-end=3D"104">1. Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"108" data-end=3D"354" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99interface graph=
ique, ou <strong data-start=3D"134" data-end=3D"168">GUI (Graphical User In=
terface)</strong>, est l=E2=80=99environnement visuel permettant aux utilis=
ateurs d=E2=80=99interagir avec leur syst=C3=A8me d=E2=80=99exploitation =
=C3=A0 l=E2=80=99aide de fen=C3=AAtres, d=E2=80=99ic=C3=B4nes et de menus, =
au lieu de la ligne de commande (CLI).</p>
<p data-start=3D"356" data-end=3D"505" class=3D"">Sous Linux, l=E2=80=99int=
erface graphique n=E2=80=99est pas monolithique comme sous Windows ou macOS=
 : elle repose sur plusieurs composants modulaires, notamment :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"665">
<li data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"552" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"552" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"508=
" data-end=3D"534">Le serveur d=E2=80=99affichage</strong> (X11, Wayland).<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"553" data-end=3D"611" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"555" data-end=3D"611" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"555=
" data-end=3D"586">Le gestionnaire de fen=C3=AAtres</strong> (Openbox, i3, =
Mutter).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"612" data-end=3D"665" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"665" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"614=
" data-end=3D"643">L=E2=80=99environnement de bureau</strong> (GNOME, KDE, =
XFCE).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"667" data-end=3D"766" class=3D"">Ce tutoriel couvre ces di=
ff=C3=A9rents aspects, du fonctionnement de base aux configurations avanc=
=C3=A9es.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"768" data-end=3D"771" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"773" data-end=3D"839" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"77=
6" data-end=3D"837">2. Serveur d=E2=80=99Affichage : Le C=C5=93ur de l=E2=
=80=99Interface Graphique</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"841" data-end=3D"1006" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D=
"844" data-end=3D"867">serveur d=E2=80=99affichage</strong> est le programm=
e qui g=C3=A8re l=E2=80=99affichage des fen=C3=AAtres et la communication a=
vec les p=C3=A9riph=C3=A9riques d=E2=80=99entr=C3=A9e (souris, clavier, =C3=
=A9cran tactile).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1008" data-end=3D"1043" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1012" data-end=3D"1041">2.1 X11 (X Window System)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1044" data-end=3D"1204">
<li data-start=3D"1044" data-end=3D"1082" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1046" data-end=3D"1082" class=3D"">Utilis=C3=A9 historique=
ment sous Linux.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1083" data-end=3D"1128" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1085" data-end=3D"1128" class=3D"">Bas=C3=A9 sur une archi=
tecture client-serveur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1129" data-end=3D"1204" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1131" data-end=3D"1204" class=3D"">Permet d=E2=80=99ex=C3=
=A9cuter des applications graphiques =C3=A0 distance via le r=C3=A9seau.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1206" data-end=3D"1227" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1210" data-end=3D"1225">2.2 Wayland</strong></h3>
