<h3 data-start=3D"3098" data-end=3D"3128" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3102" data-end=3D"3128">2.4. Limites de <code data-start=3D"3120" data-end=
=3D"3126">init</code></strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3130" data-end=3D"3563">
<li data-start=3D"3130" data-end=3D"3284" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3132" data-end=3D"3284" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
132" data-end=3D"3143">Lenteur</strong> : Le processus d'initialisation ave=
c <code data-start=3D"3181" data-end=3D"3187">init</code> peut =C3=AAtre le=
nt, surtout lorsqu'il s'agit de services complexes ou d'un grand nombre de =
services.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3285" data-end=3D"3434" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3287" data-end=3D"3434" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
287" data-end=3D"3322">Gestion des d=C3=A9pendances limit=C3=A9e</strong> :=
 <code data-start=3D"3325" data-end=3D"3331">init</code> ne g=C3=A8re pas b=
ien les d=C3=A9pendances entre les services, ce qui peut entra=C3=AEner des=
 d=C3=A9marrages inefficaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3435" data-end=3D"3563" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3437" data-end=3D"3563" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
437" data-end=3D"3463">Manque de parall=C3=A9lisme</strong> : Tous les serv=
ices sont lanc=C3=A9s s=C3=A9quentiellement, ce qui peut ralentir l'initial=
isation du syst=C3=A8me.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3565" data-end=3D"3568" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3570" data-end=3D"3617" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3573" data-end=3D"3617">3. Le syst=C3=A8me d'initialisation <code data-star=
t=3D"3606" data-end=3D"3615">systemd</code></strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3619" data-end=3D"3657" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3623" data-end=3D"3657">3.1. Qu'est-ce que <code data-start=3D"3644" data-e=
nd=3D"3653">systemd</code> ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3659" data-end=3D"3964" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"365=
9" data-end=3D"3668">systemd</code> est un syst=C3=A8me d'initialisation mo=
derne qui remplace <code data-start=3D"3722" data-end=3D"3728">init</code> =
dans la plupart des distributions Linux r=C3=A9centes. Il a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 c=
on=C3=A7u pour r=C3=A9soudre de nombreux probl=C3=A8mes rencontr=C3=A9s ave=
c <code data-start=3D"3846" data-end=3D"3852">init</code>, notamment la len=
teur du d=C3=A9marrage, la gestion des services, et la gestion des d=C3=A9p=
endances entre les services.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3966" data-end=3D"4212" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"396=
6" data-end=3D"3975">systemd</code> est bas=C3=A9 sur des <strong data-star=
t=3D"3993" data-end=3D"4003">unit=C3=A9s</strong> qui peuvent =C3=AAtre des=
 services, des montages, des sockets, des cibles, etc. Il prend en charge l=
e parall=C3=A9lisme et la gestion des d=C3=A9pendances, ce qui permet un d=
=C3=A9marrage plus rapide et plus efficace du syst=C3=A8me.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4214" data-end=3D"4249" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4218" data-end=3D"4249">3.2. Structure de <code data-start=3D"4238" data-en=
d=3D"4247">systemd</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4251" data-end=3D"4509" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"425=
1" data-end=3D"4260">systemd</code> utilise des unit=C3=A9s (unit files) po=
ur d=C3=A9finir les services et les processus syst=C3=A8me =C3=A0 g=C3=A9re=
r. Ces unit=C3=A9s sont stock=C3=A9es dans le r=C3=A9pertoire <code data-st=
art=3D"4397" data-end=3D"4419">/etc/systemd/system/</code> et <code data-st=
art=3D"4423" data-end=3D"4445">/lib/systemd/system/</code> et sont utilis=
=C3=A9es pour d=C3=A9marrer, arr=C3=AAter et g=C3=A9rer les services.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4511" data-end=3D"4554" class=3D"">Les types d'unit=C3=A9s=
 les plus courants sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4556" data-end=3D"4901">
<li data-start=3D"4556" data-end=3D"4663" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4558" data-end=3D"4663" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
558" data-end=3D"4569">service</strong> : Pour les services qui s'ex=C3=A9c=
utent en arri=C3=A8re-plan (exemple : serveur web, base de donn=C3=A9es).</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4664" data-end=3D"4765" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4666" data-end=3D"4765" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
666" data-end=3D"4676">target</strong> : Une unit=C3=A9 qui regroupe d'autr=
es unit=C3=A9s, similaire =C3=A0 un niveau d'ex=C3=A9cution dans <code data=
-start=3D"4758" data-end=3D"4764">init</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4766" data-end=3D"4849" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4768" data-end=3D"4849" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
768" data-end=3D"4778">socket</strong> : Pour les services qui s'activent =
=C3=A0 l'arriv=C3=A9e d'une connexion r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4850" data-end=3D"4901" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4852" data-end=3D"4901" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
852" data-end=3D"4861">mount</strong> : Pour monter des syst=C3=A8mes de fi=
chiers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4903" data-end=3D"4959" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4907" data-end=3D"4959">3.3. Lancer et g=C3=A9rer des services avec <code d=
ata-start=3D"4948" data-end=3D"4957">systemd</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4961" data-end=3D"5088" class=3D"">Les services sous <code=
 data-start=3D"4979" data-end=3D"4988">systemd</code> sont g=C3=A9r=C3=A9s =
avec la commande <code data-start=3D"5017" data-end=3D"5028">systemctl</cod=
e>. Voici quelques commandes de base pour g=C3=A9rer les services :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5090" data-end=3D"5118" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5095" data-end=3D"5118">D=C3=A9marrer un service</strong></h4>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"5120" data-end=3D"5167"><div=
 class=3D"contain-inline-size rounded-md border-[0.5px] border-token-border=
-medium relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary"><div class=3D"flex items=
