<h3 data-start=3D"6161" data-end=3D"6195" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6165" data-end=3D"6195">3.3. Ajuster le Swappiness</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6197" data-end=3D"6356" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
197" data-end=3D"6213"><code data-start=3D"6199" data-end=3D"6211">swappine=
ss</code></strong> est un param=C3=A8tre du noyau qui d=C3=A9termine dans q=
uelle mesure le syst=C3=A8me Linux va utiliser l'espace swap. Le param=C3=
=A8tre varie entre 0 et 100, o=C3=B9 :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6358" data-end=3D"6573">
<li data-start=3D"6358" data-end=3D"6457" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6360" data-end=3D"6457" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
360" data-end=3D"6365">0</strong> signifie que Linux essaiera d'=C3=A9viter=
 d'utiliser l'espace swap, m=C3=AAme si la RAM est utilis=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6458" data-end=3D"6573" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6460" data-end=3D"6573" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
460" data-end=3D"6467">100</strong> signifie que Linux utilisera l'espace s=
wap le plus t=C3=B4t possible, m=C3=AAme si la RAM n'est pas encore satur=
=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
</ul>
